WEBVTT

00:32.198 --> 00:36.202
FIFTIES PROFESSIONALS

01:28.254 --> 01:32.174
DAEUNGJEON HALL

01:32.258 --> 01:35.595
The Heart of the Prajna Paramita Sutra.

01:35.720 --> 01:37.555
Avalokiteshvara Bodhisattva.

01:37.638 --> 01:40.933
Deep in the practice of Perfect Wisdom

01:41.017 --> 01:43.853
clearly saw that
all five aggregates are empty.

01:55.573 --> 01:57.325
Three of our agents are dead.

01:58.492 --> 02:00.119
We're backed into a corner.

02:00.786 --> 02:03.581
NATIONAL SECURITY ADVISOR,
KWON SOON-BOK

02:03.831 --> 02:05.291
Let's call off the operation.

02:05.833 --> 02:09.420
TEAM LEADER, ANTI-COMMUNIST INVESTIGATION
TEAM, JO SEONG-WON

02:11.130 --> 02:12.131
We got intel

02:12.214 --> 02:14.759
that an NIS agent worked
with a North Korean on drugs.

02:14.842 --> 02:17.136
We spent six long months
chasing that single piece of intel.

02:18.346 --> 02:19.347
This is what we have to show for it.

02:19.430 --> 02:22.141
Our job is to work in the shadows
and serve our country.

02:23.059 --> 02:25.936
Are you just going to stand by
while one mole eats away

02:26.520 --> 02:27.521
at the country's foundations?

02:31.317 --> 02:32.777
The mole in the
National Intelligence Service.

02:33.277 --> 02:35.529
We have to catch him
and get justice for our fallen men.

02:37.740 --> 02:39.075
Do you know who it is?

02:48.167 --> 02:50.628
Han Gyeong-wook, Deputy Director
of the Anti-Communist Investigation Team.

02:51.087 --> 02:52.129
You know him well, don't you?

02:53.714 --> 02:54.715
But...

02:55.508 --> 02:58.177
why would a legend at catching spies
be working with North Korea?

02:58.302 --> 02:59.512
Isn't this disinformation?

02:59.595 --> 03:01.764
This intel cost our agents' lives.

03:02.598 --> 03:04.850
- It's solid.
- Do you have any concrete proof?

03:06.143 --> 03:07.353
Concrete proof?

03:08.479 --> 03:09.480
I have it.

03:13.109 --> 03:16.320
A few days ago, a special op from
North Korea's Counterintelligence Bureau

03:17.196 --> 03:18.781
Black Pearl, defected.

03:19.782 --> 03:21.992
She fled, stealing a slush fund
from a high-ranking North Korean official

03:22.493 --> 03:23.911
and a USB drive with data

03:24.161 --> 03:25.788
on their smuggling operations.

03:25.871 --> 03:26.997
On that drive...

03:27.081 --> 03:28.874
is information about the drug deal

03:29.125 --> 03:30.876
between Han Gyeong-wook
and the North Korean officer.

03:31.544 --> 03:33.170
If we get our hands on that USB

03:33.629 --> 03:36.090
there's no way Han Gyeong-wook
can get out of this.

03:37.258 --> 03:38.259
But...

03:38.592 --> 03:39.844
there's one problem.

03:41.178 --> 03:43.764
We tried contacting Black Pearl
through back channels

03:43.931 --> 03:45.307
but the negotiations fell apart.

03:45.391 --> 03:49.145
JAPANESE INTELLIGENCE BUREAU AGENT,
SHIBASAKI MICHIKO

03:50.896 --> 03:52.314
Black Pearl plans to sell

03:52.398 --> 03:54.692
the info to the Japanese for a high price

03:54.942 --> 03:56.235
and she's trying to get away with it.

03:59.697 --> 04:01.991
In two days,
Black Pearl's taking a ship to Japan.

04:02.575 --> 04:05.077
She'll rendezvous with the agent
on the ferry.

04:05.369 --> 04:06.746
We must intercept it before then.

04:06.829 --> 04:08.247
And if we fail?

04:09.415 --> 04:11.709
Is there another way?

04:12.877 --> 04:13.878
No.

04:18.507 --> 04:19.717
If we don't stop them this time

04:20.468 --> 04:23.179
they'll flood the country
with a massive amount of drugs.

04:23.929 --> 04:26.640
Then it'll only be a matter of time
before South Korea is a narco-state.

04:29.393 --> 04:30.478
This operation...

04:31.645 --> 04:34.106
needs someone who gets the job done,
no matter what.

04:35.357 --> 04:36.358
But...

04:37.485 --> 04:39.195
Right now, there's no one I can trust.

04:40.362 --> 04:41.614
I know just the person.

04:42.573 --> 04:46.368
Sir, are you aware that within
the National Intelligence Service...

04:46.702 --> 04:48.204
there's a unit that doesn't exist
in unofficial records?

04:55.628 --> 04:57.338
It has only one agent.

05:00.466 --> 05:01.634
Who are you?

05:01.717 --> 05:03.886
He's only deployed on missions
where everyone else has failed.

05:04.470 --> 05:06.055
The National Intelligence Service's
top black ops agent.

05:09.016 --> 05:10.100
Attack!

05:43.509 --> 05:44.760
Codename...

05:46.262 --> 05:47.346
Shadow.

05:49.348 --> 05:50.850
Even if we deploy Shadow

05:51.225 --> 05:52.977
there's still a chance
the information could leak.

05:53.477 --> 05:54.854
Chief Han's NIS network

05:55.062 --> 05:56.272
is incredibly strong.

05:56.355 --> 05:59.024
CHEONBULJEON

05:59.733 --> 06:00.818
This operation...

06:01.861 --> 06:03.362
will be conducted in absolute secrecy.

06:04.613 --> 06:06.782
Team Leader Jo, just you, me, and Shadow.

06:07.032 --> 06:08.033
Only the three of us will know.

06:10.369 --> 06:11.662
If this goes south...

06:13.664 --> 06:15.541
you could be in serious trouble, sir.

06:17.668 --> 06:19.587
To take down the great Han Gyeong-wook...

06:20.754 --> 06:22.423
I'm willing to put my own neck
on the line.

06:34.935 --> 06:36.854
I regret that things
have turned out this way.

06:37.146 --> 06:39.732
I never expected this
from that bitch Black Pearl.

06:39.899 --> 06:41.567
So, what's the solution?

06:42.234 --> 06:45.070
DEPUTY DIRECTOR, NIS
HAN GYEONG-WOOK

06:45.529 --> 06:47.948
I'll try to use some local thugs
to clean this up.

06:48.908 --> 06:51.911
MAJOR RI CHOL-JIN,
MINISTRY OF THE PEOPLE'S ARMED FORCES

06:52.494 --> 06:55.039
Shadow, the agent
assigned to this operation...

06:55.915 --> 06:57.875
is a monster raised by the NIS.

06:58.125 --> 07:00.961
A truckload of your pathetic rabble
won't make a difference.

07:02.421 --> 07:03.797
Fight a monster with a monster.

07:04.673 --> 07:05.841
On our side

07:05.966 --> 07:09.470
what if we deploy our top agent
who's skilled in South Korean ops?

07:10.054 --> 07:11.180
Your top agent?

07:19.688 --> 07:20.689
Bulgae.

07:21.315 --> 07:23.651
He's a disguise and Taekkyeon expert

07:23.984 --> 07:25.694
so his movements are phantom-like.

07:26.153 --> 07:29.031
Those weak little South Korean punks
won't be a match for him.

07:51.303 --> 07:53.889
I've never seen anyone
who could handle Bulgae.

07:56.558 --> 07:57.810
Trust me and leave it to him.

08:04.233 --> 08:05.734
I need a contingency plan.

08:07.486 --> 08:09.321
We'll go with a two-pronged operation.

08:11.573 --> 08:12.616
How interesting.

08:43.147 --> 08:45.691
BOSS OF THE HWASAN SECT
HWANG HWA-SAN

08:47.693 --> 08:49.737
Well, you didn't come here

08:49.820 --> 08:52.489
just to rehash the old days.

08:53.741 --> 08:55.284
So what is it that you want?

08:56.201 --> 08:58.203
You're still as sharp as ever
at reading the room.

08:58.454 --> 09:00.622
How about we work together again?

09:00.789 --> 09:01.832
Who is it?

09:02.041 --> 09:04.168
To make the great Chief Han...

09:04.668 --> 09:06.086
this nervous.

09:09.506 --> 09:10.758
Don't cross the line.

09:11.759 --> 09:13.927
Find me one of your guys
who can get the job done.

09:14.011 --> 09:16.055
Not some run-of-the-mill punk.

09:16.555 --> 09:17.723
I need someone who's the real deal.

09:19.933 --> 09:22.811
The real deal...

09:26.190 --> 09:29.276
I've got just the guy for you.

09:39.453 --> 09:41.622
He took down nationwide gangsters
who were armed to the teeth

09:42.039 --> 09:43.707
with his bare fists.

09:44.917 --> 09:46.502
He's a true fighter.

09:49.088 --> 09:51.090
I don't know who he's up against

09:51.757 --> 09:53.884
but one punch from my guy...

09:55.969 --> 09:57.387
will be enough to settle things.

10:41.849 --> 10:45.144
The package has top-secret documents
from our Republic.

10:45.936 --> 10:48.397
We can't let the South Korean bastards
get their hands on it, can we?

10:49.439 --> 10:50.649
In South Korea

10:51.108 --> 10:53.068
an agent called Shadow
has already been deployed.

10:54.528 --> 10:56.029
Rumor has it that bastard

10:56.405 --> 10:59.324
is the best agent in South Korea,
so be extremely careful.

11:01.326 --> 11:04.037
You must get the package before he does.

11:09.543 --> 11:10.544
Beom-ryong.

11:10.794 --> 11:12.754
What is our Hwasan Sect?

11:13.380 --> 11:14.464
Didn't we build this

11:14.548 --> 11:17.801
from nothing in Gangnam
with our bare hands?

11:18.385 --> 11:20.846
We may be taking orders
from Han Gyeong-wook

11:21.597 --> 11:24.933
but he's the type of guy
to find our weakness someday

11:25.225 --> 11:26.310
and stab us in the back.

11:26.977 --> 11:28.187
We can't trust someone like him

11:28.437 --> 11:30.439
with the fate of our organization.

11:31.565 --> 11:32.649
It doesn't matter.

11:32.774 --> 11:34.902
NIS guy or North Korean.

11:35.110 --> 11:36.153
No matter what

11:36.486 --> 11:38.614
you have to get the package

11:38.906 --> 11:39.907
first.

11:44.912 --> 11:45.913
Ho-myeong.

11:46.413 --> 11:47.414
Han Gyeong-wook

11:47.664 --> 11:51.001
has the NIS, prosecution,
and politicians in his pocket.

11:51.460 --> 11:53.212
If this continues,
the evil things he's done...

11:54.963 --> 11:56.423
could be buried forever.

11:57.257 --> 11:59.968
This is the last chance
we have to catch him.

12:02.387 --> 12:03.513
Also, for this mission

12:03.764 --> 12:05.599
there's talk that Bulgae
is being deployed.

12:06.016 --> 12:07.142
Be extra careful.

12:07.517 --> 12:10.229
And you just focus
on securing the package.

12:10.938 --> 12:11.939
Got it?

12:47.891 --> 12:48.934
This mission...

12:49.935 --> 12:51.895
is your last one as Shadow.

13:48.035 --> 13:52.247
HAN GYEONG-WOOK, DEPUTY DIRECTOR,
NATIONAL INTELLIGENCE SERVICE

13:59.880 --> 14:00.881
What's the status?

14:00.964 --> 14:01.965
Something's gone wrong.

14:02.341 --> 14:03.759
We failed to secure the package.

14:04.593 --> 14:05.802
Did Jeong Ho-myeong take it?

14:05.886 --> 14:08.013
No, sir. A North Korean agent took it.

14:08.347 --> 14:10.307
But he disappeared with the package.

14:10.849 --> 14:12.225
Erase every trace.

14:12.517 --> 14:13.643
As for the missing package...

14:14.144 --> 14:15.979
we retrieve it no matter what.

14:20.233 --> 14:21.401
Hey, Team Leader Jo.

14:21.526 --> 14:22.611
What's the status?

14:25.947 --> 14:26.948
Got it.

14:27.032 --> 14:28.075
First...

14:28.158 --> 14:29.159
get to safety.

14:29.785 --> 14:31.244
Let's meet at the safe house.

14:45.300 --> 14:46.760
The bag's GPS...

14:46.843 --> 14:49.638
The last signal from Bulgae
was on Yeongseon Island.

14:50.263 --> 14:51.515
Now the operation has gone south

14:51.598 --> 14:53.058
Han Gyeong-wook won't just stand by.

14:53.392 --> 14:55.018
I've already erased all your records.

14:55.227 --> 14:57.604
You go to Yeongseon Island
and find Bulgae, okay?

14:57.771 --> 14:58.772
Just find him.

15:00.482 --> 15:01.483
No, don't come.

15:01.775 --> 15:04.778
Don't come and just lay low
until I contact you, all right?

15:04.945 --> 15:06.238
I'll be in touch.

15:08.907 --> 15:09.908
Seong-won.

15:13.286 --> 15:14.287
Seong-won.

15:16.665 --> 15:18.166
Seong-won!

15:26.550 --> 15:31.721
FIFTIES PROFESSIONALS

15:32.389 --> 15:34.808
10 YEARS LATER

15:34.891 --> 15:38.603
YEONGSEON ISLAND

15:47.404 --> 15:48.405
Excuse me?

15:49.573 --> 15:52.325
- Can you repeat that?
- I said it's male menopause.

15:52.659 --> 15:54.494
You've heard of male menopause, right?

15:55.662 --> 15:56.663
Menopause...

15:57.330 --> 15:58.582
Can men get that too?

15:58.707 --> 16:00.292
It's common in middle-aged men

16:00.375 --> 16:02.419
with decreased male hormone levels.

16:02.627 --> 16:03.753
Hold on...

16:05.005 --> 16:07.132
I think there's been a mistake.
Could you check...

16:07.215 --> 16:09.426
Your testosterone level

16:09.926 --> 16:11.887
is currently below the threshold.

16:13.013 --> 16:15.098
For now,
I'm prescribing you male hormones.

16:15.182 --> 16:17.517
Take them regularly,
and we'll monitor your progress.

16:17.893 --> 16:20.395
- Hormones?
- If you don't treat this

16:20.729 --> 16:22.731
your symptoms will only get worse.

16:24.149 --> 16:25.400
Symptoms?

16:26.067 --> 16:27.110
Like what?

16:27.194 --> 16:28.987
Fatigue, lethargy

16:29.529 --> 16:30.864
and sexual dysfunction.

16:32.824 --> 16:34.075
You could even get shorter.

16:41.041 --> 16:42.459
You are now...

16:42.542 --> 16:45.086
ten years in the past.

16:46.129 --> 16:48.381
What do you see in front of you?

16:51.676 --> 16:53.094
People.

16:53.470 --> 16:54.721
What are you

16:54.804 --> 16:56.932
and those people doing, Je-sun?

16:58.558 --> 17:00.852
I'm fighting them. It's 17 to 1.

17:00.936 --> 17:03.146
They're no match for me.

17:07.692 --> 17:09.152
Open your eyes.

17:16.201 --> 17:17.494
It was so vivid.

17:18.537 --> 17:20.247
Are my memories coming back?

17:22.082 --> 17:25.252
I told you to stop watching
so many action movies, didn't I?

17:25.335 --> 17:28.171
You're always infiltrating some place
or defusing a bomb.

17:28.672 --> 17:29.881
The hypnosis keeps failing

17:29.965 --> 17:32.092
because it's all you ever think about.

17:32.217 --> 17:33.426
But I haven't watched any.

17:33.510 --> 17:35.720
I don't think
this hypnotherapy is working.

17:47.274 --> 17:48.316
Have you gained weight?

17:49.025 --> 17:50.569
You're looking good.

17:53.446 --> 17:54.781
Oh, well...

17:55.699 --> 17:58.368
By the way, how's your health, Boss?

17:58.451 --> 18:00.412
I heard you had a bad time with the flu.

18:00.662 --> 18:03.665
Yeah. I bought some thermals
with the money you put on my books.

18:04.624 --> 18:05.875
So I'm all better now.

18:07.252 --> 18:08.545
But the package...

18:09.379 --> 18:10.630
Still no update?

18:12.757 --> 18:14.843
I'm sorry. I've failed you.

18:15.218 --> 18:16.803
But we're searching everywhere.

18:17.053 --> 18:18.346
We should have good news soon.

18:18.555 --> 18:19.556
Okay.

18:22.726 --> 18:24.394
The Lord said it himself.

18:25.478 --> 18:27.480
"Knock, and the door will be opened."

18:27.897 --> 18:29.441
So knock. Knock until it opens.

18:29.524 --> 18:31.234
Knock! And don't give up.

18:31.401 --> 18:32.402
Amen.

18:33.111 --> 18:35.697
JUMBO 24

18:42.329 --> 18:43.413
Seoraksan.

18:44.873 --> 18:46.791
Seoraksan is a mountain
in Gangwon Province.

18:47.000 --> 18:48.209
This is Yeongseon Island.

18:48.335 --> 18:50.795
Are you being smart with me?

18:51.630 --> 18:53.548
I said I want cigarettes. Seoraksan.

18:55.842 --> 18:56.885
That brand...

18:57.218 --> 18:58.887
You're the only one who buys them

18:58.970 --> 19:00.722
so we're not stocking them anymore.

19:00.805 --> 19:02.515
I told you so many times.
Why won't you stock them?

19:04.059 --> 19:05.060
You...

19:07.812 --> 19:09.314
Do you have any idea who I am?

19:09.606 --> 19:10.607
Who might you be?

19:10.732 --> 19:12.859
- Because I have no idea.
- Damn it...

19:12.942 --> 19:14.944
- I can't hit a civilian.
- Go ahead.

19:15.362 --> 19:17.155
I'm ready to quit anyway.

19:18.573 --> 19:19.616
Look at this punk.

19:19.908 --> 19:21.493
- All right, today's your lucky day.
- What are you doing?

19:21.660 --> 19:22.661
You're in for it now.

19:23.119 --> 19:24.579
You think you're the only one
who can take something off?

19:25.246 --> 19:26.414
I can do it too.

19:26.915 --> 19:27.916
This is so stressful.

19:28.416 --> 19:29.417
Sir!

19:36.341 --> 19:37.342
Manager Bong.

19:37.425 --> 19:38.426
Yes?

19:38.510 --> 19:41.846
- Manager Bong, the toilet's clogged.
- Oh, okay.

19:42.347 --> 19:43.515
Manager Bong.

19:43.890 --> 19:45.558
The printer's out of order again.

19:46.184 --> 19:47.268
Hurry.

19:53.775 --> 19:54.776
Manager Bong.

19:56.319 --> 19:59.072
Come on, am I supposed to
handle the rebar shipment alone?

19:59.155 --> 20:00.407
No, it's just...

20:01.241 --> 20:02.742
The printer is broken.

20:18.758 --> 20:19.968
You fixed it.

20:20.677 --> 20:21.678
Thanks.

20:23.388 --> 20:24.389
Manager Bong.

20:24.973 --> 20:27.350
There's something
I've been meaning to tell you.

20:28.059 --> 20:29.769
You need to start saying no to tasks

20:29.853 --> 20:31.146
that aren't part of your job.

20:31.271 --> 20:32.272
If you always say yes

20:32.355 --> 20:33.940
they'll see you as a pushover
and pile on more work.

20:34.023 --> 20:35.024
You're right.

20:35.191 --> 20:37.402
Okay. Next time, I'll refuse point-blank.

20:38.820 --> 20:39.821
Let's hurry.

20:40.280 --> 20:41.281
Manager Bong.

20:42.365 --> 20:43.658
I'm sorry...

20:44.659 --> 20:46.202
but I'm a bit busy right now.

20:48.913 --> 20:50.290
Did I hear you correctly?

20:53.084 --> 20:54.085
You're busy?

20:59.507 --> 21:01.509
Even if you're busy,
I need you to wash my car.

21:01.926 --> 21:02.927
Make sure it's spotless.

21:13.563 --> 21:14.564
Nice pitch!

21:16.232 --> 21:17.233
Boss.

21:27.035 --> 21:28.328
That's a dead ball.

21:28.453 --> 21:30.455
That was incredibly fast, though.

21:30.538 --> 21:32.332
Gosh, sorry.

21:32.707 --> 21:36.461
My arm is so powerful I have no control.

21:42.300 --> 21:43.301
Manager Bong.

21:44.135 --> 21:46.221
There's no shine.

21:46.679 --> 21:48.056
Are you just going through the motions?

21:48.139 --> 21:49.224
I'm sorry.

21:50.225 --> 21:54.813
You really can't do anything right,
can you?

21:55.188 --> 21:58.858
What can I expect from a man
who doesn't even know who he is?

21:58.942 --> 22:01.694
God, what a half-wit.

22:02.362 --> 22:06.825
Who else but me would hire
a flawed old man?

22:07.075 --> 22:09.327
As if he knows anything. Unbelievable.

22:11.162 --> 22:12.163
Boss.

22:14.457 --> 22:15.458
What?

22:20.672 --> 22:22.257
Where should I polish?

22:23.299 --> 22:25.093
Are you joking me right now?

22:25.510 --> 22:27.887
You polish the hood, of course. The hood.

22:29.389 --> 22:31.599
Oh, for crying out loud.

22:35.019 --> 22:37.772
ORAN CHINESE RESTAURANT

22:37.856 --> 22:39.482
Can we have some more pickled radish?

22:39.566 --> 22:43.528
- Where is ours?
- The pickled radish is coming.

22:43.611 --> 22:46.698
Yes, here is your order. Enjoy.

22:47.699 --> 22:50.410
- Mr. Kim, clear table one.
- Yes, okay.

22:50.535 --> 22:51.536
- Excuse me.
- Yes?

22:51.619 --> 22:53.538
- We'd like to add a jajangmyeon.
- Yes, right away.

23:02.130 --> 23:03.131
Goodness.

23:03.423 --> 23:05.717
What took you so long?

23:05.967 --> 23:08.011
Wait, why is it only you
and my father-in-law?

23:08.511 --> 23:09.512
Where's Ji-woo's mom?

23:09.679 --> 23:11.764
She said she had a dance club meeting

23:11.848 --> 23:12.932
and left suddenly.

23:13.057 --> 23:14.100
Again?

23:14.726 --> 23:16.853
Has she gone crazy for dancing?
What's with her lately?

23:16.936 --> 23:19.230
You live with her. How would I know?

23:19.314 --> 23:20.315
Mr. Jeong, we're backed up.

23:20.398 --> 23:21.774
- Get back inside. Quickly.
- Go.

23:21.858 --> 23:23.192
- Go in.
- And clear this table.

23:23.276 --> 23:24.277
Yes, yes.

23:59.604 --> 24:00.647
What are you looking at?

24:02.440 --> 24:03.942
SPICY STIR-FRIED PORK LUNCH BOX

24:07.153 --> 24:08.363
The expired food.

24:08.446 --> 24:09.948
I'm so sick of it.

24:13.493 --> 24:14.494
Hey.

24:14.577 --> 24:16.746
You're just hangry.

24:20.833 --> 24:23.127
Come on, it's not the first time
that old geezer's been a pain.

24:23.461 --> 24:24.879
Can't you just let it slide?

24:26.130 --> 24:27.215
This is a friendly convenience store.

24:27.799 --> 24:29.217
We have to keep our reputation, you know.

24:35.515 --> 24:37.892
Boss, I can't live like this anymore.

24:38.393 --> 24:40.520
Let's find the item
and get off Yeongseon Island already.

24:41.562 --> 24:43.064
I was wondering
when you'd bring that up again.

24:43.398 --> 24:45.233
Hey, if finding the item was so easy

24:45.358 --> 24:46.776
why do you think I'd still be here?

24:46.859 --> 24:49.612
Look, what was our mission for coming
to this island in the first place?

24:49.988 --> 24:52.657
Wasn't it to stop Jeong Ho-myeong,
the NIS agent who's after the item?

24:55.159 --> 24:56.160
Look.

24:56.577 --> 24:58.454
Jeong Ho-myeong's been more active

24:58.538 --> 24:59.956
and his movements are suspicious.

25:00.039 --> 25:01.666
I'm telling you, it feels like
he's about to make a move.

25:01.749 --> 25:03.960
Are you still tailing him
from Oran Chinese Restaurant?

25:04.836 --> 25:06.045
Yeah, now and then.

25:06.337 --> 25:08.297
It's my job.

25:08.840 --> 25:11.968
Hey, that woman is happily married
and living a good life.

25:12.135 --> 25:13.928
Why on earth would he
go looking for the item?

25:14.220 --> 25:16.931
Instead of tailing him, you should be
thinking about boosting sales here.

25:17.765 --> 25:20.309
We're already spread thin just trying
to support the Boss in prison.

25:21.394 --> 25:23.521
- Does the Boss feel the same way?
- Yeah!

25:24.647 --> 25:25.940
That we should forget revenge

25:26.024 --> 25:28.067
and just focus on supporting him?

25:28.151 --> 25:29.152
Probably!

25:32.113 --> 25:33.823
Whatever you think, Boss

25:33.906 --> 25:36.075
I can't live as a convenience
store clerk anymore!

25:39.162 --> 25:40.705
Yeah? And what are you going
to do about it?

25:43.916 --> 25:44.917
Hey!

25:45.001 --> 25:48.379
JUMBO 24 FRIENDLY CONVENIENCE STORE
YEONGSEON ISLAND BRANCH WINS AWARD!

25:48.463 --> 25:51.299
WELCOME
ORAN CHINESE RESTAURANT

25:51.382 --> 25:55.178
- Yes, one large sweet and sour pork.
- The road has become much safer...

25:56.971 --> 25:58.264
And now for the next news.

25:58.389 --> 26:00.516
With the Imcheon mayoral election
just around the corner

26:00.600 --> 26:03.853
Independent Kim Seon-jung
and Saehanjin Party's Han Gyeong-wook

26:03.936 --> 26:07.023
have been campaigning fiercely in Imcheon.

26:07.106 --> 26:09.984
Reporter Kim I-yeong has more
from the heated scene.

26:10.068 --> 26:11.819
To make our Imcheon

26:11.903 --> 26:16.824
the happiest city in all of Korea

26:17.408 --> 26:19.410
I, Kim Seon-jung

26:19.494 --> 26:22.038
together with the citizens of Imcheon

26:22.330 --> 26:24.916
will lead the way.

26:24.999 --> 26:28.252
- Kim Seon-jung!
- Kim Seon-jung!

26:28.336 --> 26:29.796
Please, place your trust in me

26:29.879 --> 26:32.507
candidate number two, Han Gyeong-wook.

26:32.840 --> 26:34.300
If I, Han Gyeong-wook

26:34.383 --> 26:36.552
am elected Mayor of Imcheon

26:36.677 --> 26:39.430
by developing a large-scale
tourism complex

26:39.514 --> 26:41.015
I will make our Yeongseon Island...

26:41.390 --> 26:45.436
into South Korea's premier
tourist destination.

26:47.021 --> 26:51.943
Han Gyeong-wook!
Candidate number two, Han Gyeong-wook!

26:52.026 --> 26:57.865
Candidate number two, Han Gyeong-wook!

27:01.577 --> 27:03.079
I was watching that.
Why did you turn it off?

27:03.538 --> 27:04.664
Because it's loud.

27:04.747 --> 27:07.333
You know how vital this election is
for Yeongseon Island?

27:09.335 --> 27:11.587
Han Gyeong-wook absolutely has to
win this election

27:11.671 --> 27:14.006
but then this Kim Seon-jung guy
popped up out of nowhere.

27:15.258 --> 27:16.884
And why does it have to be
Han Gyeong-wook?

27:16.968 --> 27:19.679
I've been a deliveryman for 20 years.

27:20.304 --> 27:23.057
I can tell just by looking at someone
if they're going to ask for freebies

27:23.141 --> 27:25.184
or try to skip out on the bill.
I just know.

27:25.268 --> 27:26.310
But look at Kim Seon-jung.

27:26.686 --> 27:30.064
Do you think a bookworm teacher
can handle politics?

27:33.401 --> 27:34.652
But this Han Gyeong-wook guy

27:34.986 --> 27:37.655
he has a completely different
aura about him.

27:37.989 --> 27:40.241
He was at the National Intel Service
and a two-term congressman.

27:40.324 --> 27:43.119
If Han Gyeong-wook gets elected

27:43.202 --> 27:44.996
and makes Yeongseon Island
a special tourist zone

27:45.288 --> 27:49.458
- this place will skyrocket.
- Stop the chit-chat, huh?

27:49.542 --> 27:50.543
Ho-myeong.

27:51.169 --> 27:52.336
Go make a delivery.

27:52.962 --> 27:54.630
Mr. Kim should go.

27:54.714 --> 27:56.090
I have to prep for the dinner rush.

27:56.174 --> 27:57.216
That place...

27:57.508 --> 28:00.011
- is a place Mr. Kim can't go.
- What do you mean?

28:02.847 --> 28:04.557
- Heaven Capital?
- That's the one.

28:05.349 --> 28:08.227
The one where Mr. Kim gets credit
every time he goes.

28:08.561 --> 28:10.271
You're kidding. He has a tab there?

28:10.354 --> 28:11.814
With 20 years of experience?

28:13.232 --> 28:14.525
Since you're going, Ho-myeong

28:14.734 --> 28:16.777
collect all their overdue payments.

28:17.153 --> 28:19.113
O-ran's checking the books today.

28:19.197 --> 28:20.656
If she sees a hole in our sales

28:20.740 --> 28:22.074
do you think she'll let it slide?

28:23.868 --> 28:25.661
You think Ho-myeong
can collect from those guys?

28:26.078 --> 28:28.247
Not a chance. If he does, I'll eat my hat.

28:28.998 --> 28:29.999
You would've had to

28:30.208 --> 28:32.251
eat your hat 90 times by now.

28:34.212 --> 28:36.297
IMCHEON

28:36.380 --> 28:38.382
The case was closed as a suicide.

28:38.466 --> 28:40.092
Why is the prosecution
trying to reopen it?

28:40.509 --> 28:42.803
Didn't Park promise to handle it

28:42.887 --> 28:44.388
without a problem?

28:44.472 --> 28:46.432
After Prosecutor Park's promotion

28:46.515 --> 28:48.059
a new one just arrived, right?

28:48.142 --> 28:51.437
The new prosecutor is making a fuss,
insisting on seeing the crime scene.

28:51.520 --> 28:52.521
A new prosecutor?

28:53.147 --> 28:54.774
You don't think
they're onto something, do you?

28:56.108 --> 28:58.152
She can't catch on
if there's nothing to catch on to.

28:58.653 --> 28:59.904
What is she going to do about it now?

29:02.657 --> 29:04.116
Still, don't let your guard down.

29:04.784 --> 29:06.494
Do you know that prosecutor's nickname?

29:06.869 --> 29:07.870
What is it?

29:08.329 --> 29:09.580
They call her Nongae.

29:09.664 --> 29:10.706
You know Nongae, right?

29:10.915 --> 29:12.959
The courtesan jumped in the river,
taking a Japanese general with her.

29:13.584 --> 29:16.254
Once she sinks her teeth into a case,
she takes everyone down with her.

29:16.671 --> 29:17.880
She's a police academy graduate

29:17.964 --> 29:19.465
and worked violent crime for years.

29:20.007 --> 29:21.759
And she was known
as a total psycho there, too.

29:22.385 --> 29:24.595
Even after becoming a prosecutor,
old habits die hard.

29:24.887 --> 29:27.515
She even went after her own superior
for sexual harassment

29:27.598 --> 29:29.934
And rumor is she was demoted for that to
the Imcheon District Prosecutors' Office.

29:30.017 --> 29:31.686
Actually, it's a fact.

29:32.979 --> 29:33.980
Hello.

29:34.063 --> 29:36.774
I'm Prosecutor Gang Yeong-ae from the
Imcheon District Prosecutors' Office.

29:36.857 --> 29:38.818
- It's a pleasure to meet you.
- Yes, a pleasure.

29:38.901 --> 29:42.238
- Right.
- I'm sorry. I didn't mean to gossip.

29:42.488 --> 29:44.949
Don't be. Why apologize
for stating a fact?

29:46.409 --> 29:47.535
Shall we go up?

29:50.204 --> 29:51.247
Don't you have work to do?

29:54.375 --> 29:55.793
Prosecutor.

29:55.876 --> 29:57.253
Wait, Prosecutor!

29:57.753 --> 30:01.299
- Chairman Do must step down!
- Step down!

30:01.382 --> 30:06.012
- No casino on Yeongseon Island!
- Out!

30:06.095 --> 30:09.390
Chairman Do of Heaven Casino,
pull out now!

30:09.473 --> 30:12.059
Pull out!

30:12.143 --> 30:15.354
The gambling that's bleeding
us dry must go!

30:15.688 --> 30:18.024
Go!

30:18.107 --> 30:21.569
What's a casino doing
in pristine Yeongseon Island?

30:40.755 --> 30:42.089
Welcome.

31:17.833 --> 31:19.210
HEAVEN CAPITAL

31:25.549 --> 31:26.926
I want a taste of heaven too.

31:27.009 --> 31:28.969
Hey, one more round.

31:29.261 --> 31:30.888
You crazy bastard, I'm all out!

31:32.890 --> 31:34.350
You've got to get to heaven, right?

31:35.559 --> 31:37.019
- You can make it.
- No!

31:37.603 --> 31:39.522
No way. What? This is wrong.

31:42.566 --> 31:44.985
Look how you have to bend it. See?
He bent his card just like this.

31:45.528 --> 31:47.446
- Believe me, he bent it like this.
- Delivery!

31:48.614 --> 31:49.824
Hey, over here.

31:51.450 --> 31:52.618
Here you go.

31:52.952 --> 31:53.994
Oh, yes.

31:54.328 --> 31:55.746
Thank you.

31:58.416 --> 31:59.625
Count these.

32:04.213 --> 32:05.798
Hey, the food's here.
Let's eat and then play.

32:05.881 --> 32:07.007
- Yes, sir.
- Yes.

32:08.008 --> 32:09.510
- Hey, clear this stuff.
- Yes, sir.

32:14.098 --> 32:16.517
- What are you doing?
- Including your order

32:16.600 --> 32:18.811
and your outstanding tab,
that'll be 578,000 won.

32:18.936 --> 32:20.229
You can settle your bill first.

32:20.771 --> 32:23.023
Damn, you just made me lose my appetite.

32:23.107 --> 32:24.775
I don't have any money.
Just put it on my tab.

32:26.026 --> 32:28.446
And what's that over there? Scrap paper?

32:30.531 --> 32:31.532
What the hell...

32:32.783 --> 32:33.784
You little punk.

32:33.868 --> 32:35.286
Do you know what that money is for?

32:35.369 --> 32:37.663
If a single bill goes missing,
all hell will break loose in here.

32:38.998 --> 32:41.417
We'll pay you next time,
so just go. All right?

32:46.547 --> 32:48.924
Damn, this punk just won't listen.

32:49.925 --> 32:52.803
What, do you want a beating so bad
your ears will pop?

33:03.189 --> 33:04.648
Hey, what are you doing?

33:15.159 --> 33:16.577
Damn it.

33:19.830 --> 33:21.790
Jeez. Just a nobody.

33:22.541 --> 33:23.751
Acting all tough.

33:23.959 --> 33:25.878
If you don't pay next time...

33:28.088 --> 33:29.298
I won't be making any more deliveries.

33:29.381 --> 33:32.510
Hey, bring more pickled radish
next time, you asshole.

33:32.593 --> 33:34.512
And bring some free fried dumplings.

33:34.970 --> 33:37.264
- We're regulars.
- Hey, don't talk to him like that.

33:37.389 --> 33:38.390
He looks older up close.

33:38.474 --> 33:41.268
Yeah. You should show
some respect. Thanks, mister.

33:41.769 --> 33:43.812
Give us lots of extras next time.

33:43.896 --> 33:45.064
Please bring them.

33:45.898 --> 33:47.775
You punk, just shut up and eat.

34:02.289 --> 34:03.958
Newspapers layered over the window

34:04.041 --> 34:06.335
as if to block the outside world.

34:07.336 --> 34:08.837
The room was tidy

34:08.921 --> 34:10.798
as if ready to leave at any moment.

34:10.881 --> 34:12.383
Excuse me, Prosecutor.

34:12.466 --> 34:15.469
But it was already ruled a suicide.

34:15.761 --> 34:18.138
Is there really a reason
to look into it again?

34:23.936 --> 34:25.062
Why?

34:25.854 --> 34:28.023
Why are you so sure it was a suicide? Why?

34:28.774 --> 34:29.775
Well, I mean...

34:30.359 --> 34:32.653
It's pretty obvious, isn't it?

34:32.945 --> 34:34.822
A woman who lives alone, right?

34:34.905 --> 34:36.490
She doesn't really see anyone

34:36.824 --> 34:39.034
gets depressed, and hangs herself.

34:39.410 --> 34:42.413
There's no need to brief this case, right?

34:42.663 --> 34:44.039
Going by the scene

34:44.123 --> 34:45.374
just as the detectives said

34:45.457 --> 34:48.210
it looks like a premeditated suicide
caused by depression.

34:48.460 --> 34:49.461
But...

34:49.837 --> 34:51.672
would someone who has been
contemplating their own death

34:51.755 --> 34:53.924
commit suicide
without leaving a single note?

34:54.633 --> 34:56.802
And suddenly, while doing the dishes?

35:11.525 --> 35:12.526
Prosecutor.

35:13.694 --> 35:15.946
If you've seen enough, we should go.

35:16.655 --> 35:17.906
We have to get going.

35:17.990 --> 35:20.034
The detectives are acting odd too.

35:20.284 --> 35:22.244
It's just a simple suicide case

35:22.411 --> 35:24.288
but they're being unusually wary of me.

35:24.663 --> 35:28.292
You said she fought with her neighbor
over noise complaints, right?

35:31.837 --> 35:32.838
That's right.

35:33.505 --> 35:36.258
She would come upstairs
at the slightest noise

35:36.634 --> 35:39.720
and scream and make a scene
while we were live.

35:42.014 --> 35:44.892
So you must have fought often?

35:45.267 --> 35:46.268
Are you suspecting me?

35:46.769 --> 35:48.562
Do you even know
what kind of woman she was?

35:48.854 --> 35:50.481
One, two, three, four.

35:50.564 --> 35:52.107
One, two, three, four.

35:52.274 --> 35:54.568
Wave, wave, wave.

35:54.652 --> 35:56.236
Now, jump!

36:00.824 --> 36:01.867
Damn it.

36:02.451 --> 36:03.702
Hang on, everyone.

36:06.121 --> 36:07.122
Who is it?

36:09.833 --> 36:11.001
BEST 30 UPBEAT WORKOUT SONGS

36:12.169 --> 36:14.546
I told you what would happen
if you stomped around again!

36:15.631 --> 36:17.591
What are you doing? We're live right now!

36:18.175 --> 36:19.301
What are you doing?

36:19.927 --> 36:20.928
Boss.

36:21.595 --> 36:23.931
What are you doing? Stop her, quick!

36:24.014 --> 36:25.766
What the? Hey, lady.

36:25.849 --> 36:26.850
What are you doing, lady?

36:28.060 --> 36:29.061
Are you okay?

36:29.353 --> 36:30.688
That bitch.

36:31.021 --> 36:32.022
Lady.

36:33.190 --> 36:34.316
Boss!

36:43.826 --> 36:44.868
Even now

36:45.202 --> 36:46.620
if I lift anything over 5kg

36:46.704 --> 36:48.622
my right shoulder dislocates.

36:49.039 --> 36:51.417
So how could I have killed her?

36:51.500 --> 36:53.085
I don't have the strength.

36:53.585 --> 36:55.379
- Did you press charges?
- I was going to...

36:55.796 --> 36:57.256
but the video we filmed that day...

36:58.090 --> 36:59.633
...went viral.

36:59.883 --> 37:00.884
See?

37:00.968 --> 37:02.845
What are you doing? We're live!

37:03.554 --> 37:04.596
Oh, come on.

37:06.098 --> 37:07.099
Boss.

37:07.224 --> 37:08.267
See the number of views?

37:08.350 --> 37:09.685
It's 2.53 million.

37:10.769 --> 37:11.979
It even made it to the trending page.

37:12.688 --> 37:13.689
What are you doing, lady?

37:13.897 --> 37:16.942
This video being uploaded to NewTube...

37:17.943 --> 37:19.236
did the woman know about it?

37:19.319 --> 37:21.905
My goodness, if she had known,
she'd have torn off my other one too.

37:27.035 --> 37:30.497
Prosecutor, we might start getting
complaints from the residents.

37:30.581 --> 37:33.542
- This might be a good time...
- Should we get going?

37:33.667 --> 37:34.877
Yes, we should probably go...

37:35.127 --> 37:36.378
What? You're leaving?

37:36.795 --> 37:39.506
Really? You're not going to
call us in again, right?

37:39.590 --> 37:41.091
Why would I do that?

37:41.467 --> 37:42.593
We're all busy people.

37:42.676 --> 37:44.052
I'll get going now.

37:44.136 --> 37:45.345
Okay. Thank you for your time.

37:45.596 --> 37:47.055
Yes, take care.

37:47.139 --> 37:49.183
I'll come by to greet you properly later.

37:54.855 --> 37:56.231
Oh, yes, it's me.

37:56.315 --> 37:58.192
ßYou don't need to worry.

38:18.086 --> 38:20.422
REBIRTH BY YOON JONG-SHIN

38:39.024 --> 38:41.068
SPICY STIR-FRIED PORK LUNCH BOX

38:45.239 --> 38:47.324
SPICY STIR-FRIED PORK LUNCH BOX

40:10.741 --> 40:13.368
You always have
spicy stir-fried pork lunch box left.

40:13.452 --> 40:14.953
It's sold out everywhere else.

40:15.287 --> 40:16.288
Oh...

40:17.039 --> 40:18.040
I see.

40:19.082 --> 40:21.543
For us, having too much stock
is the problem.

40:23.086 --> 40:25.255
By any chance, is there something else

40:26.381 --> 40:27.382
like another lunch box...

40:28.342 --> 40:30.135
that you'd like to eat?

40:39.603 --> 40:42.439
I'm just asking for market research.

40:43.357 --> 40:44.358
That's all.

40:47.277 --> 40:48.278
Fried chicken with sweet sauce.

40:49.613 --> 40:50.697
Fried chicken with sweet sauce?

40:50.781 --> 40:52.074
You don't have that, I assume?

40:53.075 --> 40:54.660
That's okay. I'm ready to pay.

41:03.794 --> 41:04.795
SECURITY ADVISOR HWANG:
ACCUSED OF MURDER

41:04.878 --> 41:05.879
ARREST WARRANT ISSUED
TRANSFER TODAY

41:05.963 --> 41:07.089
JEONG HO-MYEONG

41:10.884 --> 41:12.511
INTERIOR PHOTO
THE FRIED DUMPLINGS ARE DELICIOUS

41:29.277 --> 41:31.947
ORAN CHINESE RESTAURANT

41:32.030 --> 41:33.615
All right, Jeong Ho-myeong.

41:34.408 --> 41:35.867
It's time to move.

41:37.244 --> 41:38.578
Please move.

41:40.497 --> 41:41.498
Move.

41:44.918 --> 41:46.545
Gosh, this tastes great.

41:52.467 --> 41:55.387
HANMAEUM SOCIAL DANCE

41:58.056 --> 42:00.308
Honey, you're leaving
the restaurant empty every day

42:00.559 --> 42:03.437
for that K-pop thing or whatever. Why?

42:03.729 --> 42:04.730
Why?

42:06.273 --> 42:07.274
You got a problem with it?

42:08.442 --> 42:09.484
No.

42:10.902 --> 42:12.696
It's not that I have a problem...

42:13.739 --> 42:15.824
but your back has been bad
since you had Ji-woo

42:16.199 --> 42:17.993
and I get worried

42:18.076 --> 42:20.245
that you're going to throw it out dancing.

42:20.454 --> 42:22.456
Dancing is my physical therapy.
Don't you worry about it.

42:28.336 --> 42:29.921
Well, even so...

42:30.547 --> 42:33.842
wouldn't it be better to look
into some other form of therapy?

42:34.009 --> 42:36.762
Preferably one that
doesn't affect business.

42:36.845 --> 42:37.846
- Dad.
- Yeah?

42:38.638 --> 42:41.767
The dance club is a huge
help to the restaurant.

42:42.059 --> 42:44.686
With sales down and tourism slow

42:44.770 --> 42:46.772
my club's ladies brought friends

42:46.855 --> 42:49.024
and brought their families here
for dinner. Don't you remember?

42:51.193 --> 42:53.653
So my daughter had
a good reason after all.

42:53.737 --> 42:56.490
Well, then you have to go. You have to go.

43:02.329 --> 43:03.497
What... what is this?

43:04.081 --> 43:05.082
Heaven Capital?

43:07.000 --> 43:08.001
A tab?

43:11.755 --> 43:12.798
Dad.

43:12.881 --> 43:15.592
Didn't I tell you
not to take their orders?

43:15.675 --> 43:17.344
Well, it's just that...

43:17.427 --> 43:19.513
turning away customers

43:19.596 --> 43:22.557
just doesn't sit right with me.

43:22.641 --> 43:24.559
And I thought I could make them pay.

43:24.684 --> 43:26.937
- So I took it for that reason...
- And?

43:27.562 --> 43:29.356
- You put it on their tab again?
- Well...

43:31.483 --> 43:34.361
- Ho-myeong said he could handle it.
- He said that.

43:34.444 --> 43:37.697
He said he could collect
all of their old debt too.

43:37.781 --> 43:38.782
When did I say that?

43:39.074 --> 43:41.034
Father, you can't just say that.

43:41.118 --> 43:42.828
Do you think we can run tabs?

43:47.082 --> 43:48.125
Everyone, listen up.

43:48.375 --> 43:50.085
We need to get our act together, okay?

43:50.168 --> 43:51.461
If we keep going on like this

43:51.545 --> 43:52.963
we'll lose this restaurant in a heartbeat.

43:53.046 --> 43:56.800
No, I'm working hard,
so is your dad and so is he.

43:56.883 --> 43:58.510
- I work hard.
- But it's not enough.

43:58.593 --> 44:00.345
- You have to do a good job.

44:02.264 --> 44:03.265
And you.

44:03.682 --> 44:06.059
At your age, what other job
do you think you can get?

44:06.309 --> 44:07.853
Nothing, right?

44:07.936 --> 44:09.980
We have to make this restaurant work.

44:10.105 --> 44:12.774
So we can send Ji-woo to college
when we're older.

44:12.858 --> 44:14.943
Hey, that's enough! Come on...

44:18.196 --> 44:19.739
Sit down.

44:22.159 --> 44:23.160
I'm just going to take out the trash.

44:25.370 --> 44:26.955
No, I was going to do that.

44:27.038 --> 44:28.373
- Do it after you eat.
- Ho-myeong.

44:45.682 --> 44:46.725
AUTHORIZED PERSONNEL ONLY

45:30.435 --> 45:32.145
PRESCRIPTION MEDICATION INSTRUCTIONS

45:34.189 --> 45:36.441
SIDE EFFECTS MAY INCREASE
WITH ALCOHOL CONSUMPTION

46:07.222 --> 46:09.641
NO SIGNAL

48:36.121 --> 48:37.122
NIS DEPUTY HAN GYEONG-WOOK
UNCOVERS TRUTH!

48:37.205 --> 48:38.665
NIS AGENT EXPOSES HWASAN SECT
BEHIND KWON SOON-BOK'S DEATH

48:38.832 --> 48:40.083
National Intelligence Service.

48:40.667 --> 48:41.876
A ferry.

48:42.210 --> 48:44.379
MISSING NIS AGENT CASE EXPOSES FLAWS
IN THE AGENCY'S MANAGEMENT

48:45.338 --> 48:47.006
Kwon Soon-bok.

48:56.808 --> 48:59.477
YEONGSEON ISLAND

49:03.314 --> 49:05.316
Yeongseon Island.

49:06.401 --> 49:09.070
YEONGSEON ISLAND

49:16.744 --> 49:18.121
Where is Jeong Ho-myeong?

49:34.679 --> 49:38.683
YEONGSEON 5-DAY MARKET OPEN!
A TRADITIONAL MARKET WITH EVERYTHING!

49:41.478 --> 49:42.812
UNBELIEVABLE PRICES!
MARKET SPECIALS AND FREEBIES!

49:42.896 --> 49:43.897
MEET NEIGHBORS, ENJOY THE DAY!

49:55.825 --> 49:57.869
When you were found
after losing your memory

49:58.244 --> 50:00.371
you were wearing women's
clothing, correct?

50:00.830 --> 50:02.207
About that clothing...

50:02.457 --> 50:04.918
have you tried wearing it since then?

50:05.001 --> 50:07.170
Why would I wear women's clothing?

50:07.545 --> 50:09.756
Instead of just rejecting the idea

50:10.340 --> 50:12.509
why not give it a try?

50:14.052 --> 50:16.429
Your past gender identity

50:16.638 --> 50:19.015
could be the key to
unlocking your memories.

50:20.183 --> 50:21.226
The key.

50:25.605 --> 50:27.023
This looks awful on me.

50:29.984 --> 50:31.653
- Nam-il?
- Who are you?

50:31.736 --> 50:33.821
- You came home? Good.
- Stay away! Don't come any closer!

50:37.534 --> 50:38.743
What in the world are you wearing?

50:40.245 --> 50:42.247
Well, I'm just trying
to get my memory back.

50:42.372 --> 50:44.082
No, that's enough. Don't say it.

50:44.457 --> 50:45.792
I don't want to know.

50:46.000 --> 50:47.877
No, it's not what you think.
Just listen to me.

50:47.961 --> 50:49.754
Don't come closer. Stay away. Please.

50:54.842 --> 50:56.594
- Hey, Nam-il. I just...
- Talk from there.

50:57.554 --> 50:58.555
Right where you are.

50:59.597 --> 51:01.266
You've known me for ten years
and you still don't know me?

51:01.724 --> 51:03.476
Stop with the "uncle" this, "uncle" that.

51:03.560 --> 51:05.853
Stop trying to act all friendly.
It's so annoying.

51:07.730 --> 51:10.024
My grandpa only took you in
because he has a good heart.

51:11.150 --> 51:12.193
But I'm not falling for it.

51:14.112 --> 51:16.531
Why should I trust some sketchy guy
and call you "uncle"?

51:18.283 --> 51:20.410
We'll talk about that later.

51:21.452 --> 51:22.829
Why aren't you in school?

51:22.912 --> 51:24.747
Why haven't you been coming home?

51:26.249 --> 51:28.209
Who'd want to live in a dump like this?

51:29.752 --> 51:32.046
If I could just hit the jackpot once

51:32.130 --> 51:34.132
I'd be out of this dump for good.

51:34.799 --> 51:35.800
Slots?

51:36.843 --> 51:37.844
Are you gambling?

51:40.263 --> 51:41.264
What?

51:42.098 --> 51:43.099
Why?

51:44.183 --> 51:46.060
Hey, Nam-il! Get out here!

51:46.644 --> 51:48.354
Whatever. Just stay out of my business.

51:48.438 --> 51:50.356
Hey, Nam-il, where are you going?
We need to talk.

51:50.440 --> 51:52.275
Gosh, my knee... Nam-il!

51:53.067 --> 51:54.068
Where are you going?

51:54.819 --> 51:56.070
Where are you going?

51:57.238 --> 51:58.323
Just put some pants on.

52:05.371 --> 52:06.372
He didn't...

52:21.971 --> 52:23.431
The deed to the house...

52:30.938 --> 52:33.858
Try to catch it!

52:34.817 --> 52:36.402
Come on, catch it!

52:36.611 --> 52:37.820
Come on.

52:38.613 --> 52:41.282
Seriously? Are you joking with me?

52:41.658 --> 52:43.409
I don't want it anymore.

52:48.373 --> 52:49.707
I don't understand them.

52:52.752 --> 52:53.753
Give me one.

52:56.047 --> 52:57.256
One second.

53:08.434 --> 53:09.435
Take it.

53:11.104 --> 53:12.105
Take it.

53:12.814 --> 53:13.815
Take it.

53:13.898 --> 53:15.441
Stop messing with me.

53:15.525 --> 53:16.526
Come on, take it.

53:17.610 --> 53:18.611
Go on.

53:18.778 --> 53:20.321
Take it!

53:22.907 --> 53:23.908
Here.

53:24.117 --> 53:25.159
Oh, come on. Geez.

53:25.410 --> 53:26.411
Alright.

53:31.749 --> 53:32.750
What's the occasion?

53:32.834 --> 53:34.043
It's not our rendezvous day.

53:34.711 --> 53:35.712
Rendezvous?

53:36.379 --> 53:38.798
Since when does a rendezvous
require an appointment?

53:40.383 --> 53:43.886
Ever since you got married,
you're getting sloppier by the day.

53:43.970 --> 53:45.471
Try being on standby for ten years.

53:45.680 --> 53:47.014
See if you can stay sharp.

53:47.390 --> 53:49.809
Enough with that
and get to the point. I'm busy.

53:50.601 --> 53:51.853
You know Black Pearl, right?

53:52.895 --> 53:53.896
Black Pearl?

53:55.481 --> 53:56.482
Did you find her?

53:56.566 --> 53:57.567
We found her.

54:00.236 --> 54:01.779
She's been in a villa in Imcheon

54:01.863 --> 54:04.240
ever since that day ten years ago.

54:08.161 --> 54:09.912
Why was she hiding out in South Korea?

54:10.079 --> 54:11.080
I don't know.

54:11.372 --> 54:13.958
Maybe she was looking
for the item, just like us.

54:17.378 --> 54:19.213
So what did you find out?

54:19.464 --> 54:20.465
Nothing.

54:20.798 --> 54:21.924
She was found dead.

54:22.842 --> 54:24.886
- How?
- Officially, it's suicide.

54:24.969 --> 54:26.262
But I suspect murder.

54:26.888 --> 54:28.931
When this video was uploaded to NewTube

54:29.015 --> 54:30.433
I think her location was exposed.

54:32.477 --> 54:34.687
It's unlikely the North
is making a move now.

54:36.105 --> 54:38.024
- It was Han Gyeong-wook, wasn't it?
- No, we don't know yet.

54:38.107 --> 54:40.485
What do you mean, no?
You think Han Gyeong-wook is forgetful?

54:45.448 --> 54:47.116
We can't just sit around and do nothing.

54:47.533 --> 54:49.035
Shouldn't we be making a move now too?

54:49.118 --> 54:50.495
No. It's too soon.

54:52.163 --> 54:54.207
A prosecutor has started sniffing
around this case.

54:54.665 --> 54:57.084
I'm keeping an eye on her,
so just wait a little longer.

54:57.293 --> 54:58.294
- Seong-won.
- Listen.

54:58.753 --> 55:00.630
Don't you know how high up
Han Gyeong-wook is going to get?

55:00.713 --> 55:02.840
If we act rashly and expose our location

55:02.924 --> 55:04.634
then it's really over for us. You get me?

55:04.759 --> 55:06.636
So we should just keep sitting
on our hands?

55:06.719 --> 55:07.720
Doesn't this frustrate you at all?

55:07.804 --> 55:10.223
Then go find the location
of Bulgae and the item.

55:10.556 --> 55:12.099
I've told you over and over.

55:12.183 --> 55:15.394
If they were on Yeongseon Island,
I would've found them by now.

55:15.478 --> 55:16.771
The receiver was broken

55:16.854 --> 55:19.106
and Bulgae must have drowned.

55:19.190 --> 55:20.525
Hey, Ho-myeong.

55:22.068 --> 55:25.863
Let's just do something
before it's too late, okay?

55:25.947 --> 55:26.948
I...

55:27.824 --> 55:29.033
Recently, I...

55:33.913 --> 55:35.414
was diagnosed with male menopause.

55:37.208 --> 55:38.334
So you're saying...

55:38.751 --> 55:40.711
all these flare-ups...

55:41.379 --> 55:44.298
and whining are symptoms of menopause?

55:44.590 --> 55:45.591
I don't know.

55:46.717 --> 55:49.595
Sometimes I feel completely drained,
and other times I just get anxious.

55:50.054 --> 55:52.473
The doctor prescribed
some hormone medication

55:52.557 --> 55:54.183
but it doesn't seem to be helping much.

55:54.684 --> 55:55.685
Look.

55:56.727 --> 55:58.020
We're running out of time.

55:58.479 --> 56:00.982
If I keep going like this, I feel like...

56:01.983 --> 56:04.652
I won't be able to get anything done.

56:19.333 --> 56:21.168
PICK UP JI-WOO FROM KINDERGARTEN

56:21.752 --> 56:23.045
Do you have to go pick him up?

56:23.838 --> 56:24.839
Then go.

56:26.299 --> 56:28.092
Go on. I'll give you a call.

56:46.319 --> 56:49.739
YEONGSEON HAENGBOK KINDERGARTEN

56:49.822 --> 56:51.782
One by one. Let's get on on at a time.

57:13.804 --> 57:14.805
Ji-woo.

57:15.348 --> 57:16.349
Hey, Dad.

57:19.143 --> 57:21.187
Should we send you
to an academy too, Ji-woo?

57:21.479 --> 57:22.605
No.

57:22.688 --> 57:24.231
If I go to an academy

57:24.565 --> 57:27.193
you'd have to sell
a hundred bowls of jajangmyeon.

57:27.485 --> 57:30.029
Hey, don't worry about that.
Dad can sell a hundred bowls.

57:30.196 --> 57:31.614
But that's hard on you.

57:32.198 --> 57:33.199
It's okay.

57:42.249 --> 57:43.250
Dad.

57:49.382 --> 57:50.549
Do you...

57:51.133 --> 57:52.134
want this?

57:57.431 --> 57:59.600
Oh, isn't this your favorite

57:59.684 --> 58:01.018
Masked Racer?

58:01.352 --> 58:03.646
Yeah. When you wear it

58:03.729 --> 58:04.772
you get super strong.

58:05.147 --> 58:06.857
This is to cheer you up.

58:09.527 --> 58:10.528
Let's go.

58:41.392 --> 58:42.768
Wel...

58:48.399 --> 58:49.608
...come.

58:51.110 --> 58:52.695
The usual, right?

59:02.913 --> 59:04.040
- Dad.
- Yeah?

59:04.165 --> 59:05.708
He's here. The "Oldboy."

59:06.208 --> 59:07.293
You mean the fried dumpling guy?

59:08.127 --> 59:09.462
I haven't seen him in a while.

59:22.391 --> 59:23.434
Welcome.

59:25.478 --> 59:26.687
We need to talk.

59:29.065 --> 59:30.066
What is it?

59:32.193 --> 59:33.819
About Ji-woo.

59:34.779 --> 59:35.780
Let's enroll him here.

59:37.531 --> 59:38.616
ANDREW ENGLISH

59:38.699 --> 59:39.909
WHAT MAKES ANDREW ENGLISH CLASSES SPECIAL

59:41.535 --> 59:42.620
Oh, forget it.

59:43.037 --> 59:44.872
We don't have the money
for an academy already.

59:45.247 --> 59:46.499
We can send him when he's older.

59:46.582 --> 59:47.625
Hey, Kwon O-ran.

59:48.084 --> 59:49.502
Can't we do this one thing for him?

59:49.668 --> 59:51.212
All of Ji-woo's friends go here.

59:51.295 --> 59:52.755
Of course I want to.

59:52.838 --> 59:54.715
But can you afford it?

59:54.799 --> 59:56.884
You can't even increase our sales.
Don't be ridiculous.

01:00:08.104 --> 01:00:10.564
Thank you for calling
Oran Chinese Restaurant.

01:00:12.149 --> 01:00:13.150
Sorry?

01:00:16.403 --> 01:00:18.072
I understand. Got it.

01:00:19.782 --> 01:00:21.325
- A delivery? To where?
- Heaven Capital.

01:00:21.784 --> 01:00:23.619
- Heaven Capital.
- Heaven Capital?

01:00:24.995 --> 01:00:26.705
I told you not to take their orders!

01:00:26.789 --> 01:00:28.958
Why not?
We need to increase sales, don't we?

01:00:29.291 --> 01:00:31.043
I'll just collect all the money
they owe us.

01:00:31.127 --> 01:00:33.963
Come on, how will you collect from them?

01:00:34.046 --> 01:00:35.422
You go then.

01:00:35.506 --> 01:00:37.466
- Yes, you go.
- No way. I'm not going.

01:00:37.591 --> 01:00:38.968
Why not? You go.

01:00:39.051 --> 01:00:40.886
Why are you asking me?
Just send Ho-myeong.

01:00:40.970 --> 01:00:42.096
Come on, you can go.

01:00:42.179 --> 01:00:44.098
I said I don't want to.
Why do you keep trying to make me?

01:00:44.181 --> 01:00:47.268
- You said you could!
- I said, I'll go!

01:00:53.190 --> 01:00:54.525
I'm telling you.

01:00:55.192 --> 01:00:57.027
I'll collect everything they owe.

01:00:57.820 --> 01:00:58.821
Just watch and see

01:00:58.988 --> 01:01:00.614
if I can do it or not.

01:01:01.365 --> 01:01:02.366
You just watch.

01:01:03.492 --> 01:01:04.535
Those eyes...

01:01:04.952 --> 01:01:07.163
Those aren't the eyes of the cook
I've been seeing.

01:01:11.125 --> 01:01:13.127
They're the eyes I saw
on that ferry ten years ago.

01:01:13.502 --> 01:01:15.254
The eyes of a National
Intelligence Service agent.

01:01:39.612 --> 01:01:41.155
Welcome.

01:01:41.488 --> 01:01:43.365
- Welcome.
- Oh, that's all right.

01:02:09.683 --> 01:02:10.684
Seriously.

01:02:15.105 --> 01:02:16.106
Oh?

01:02:24.323 --> 01:02:25.699
Where are the house deeds?

01:02:26.408 --> 01:02:27.409
The deeds?

01:02:28.285 --> 01:02:30.246
- What about them?
- Don't you know what that house is?

01:02:30.704 --> 01:02:33.040
Grandpa built that house himself.

01:02:33.624 --> 01:02:35.167
So what if he did?

01:02:35.376 --> 01:02:37.878
The support beams are rotten
and it could collapse any day now.

01:02:38.379 --> 01:02:40.714
Better to put it to good use
before it falls apart.

01:02:41.090 --> 01:02:42.174
Don't tell me...

01:02:44.927 --> 01:02:47.346
I thought of it as a gift
from Grandpa in heaven...

01:02:47.429 --> 01:02:48.764
and cashed it in right away. What?

01:02:49.056 --> 01:02:50.057
That's a lie.

01:02:50.140 --> 01:02:51.725
- You're lying.
- Oh, come on.

01:02:52.184 --> 01:02:53.352
You'll jinx it.

01:02:54.937 --> 01:02:57.231
If this pays off,
we'll make a hundred times our money.

01:02:57.523 --> 01:02:58.565
When it does

01:02:58.983 --> 01:03:01.360
I'll buy you a kick-ass new apartment

01:03:01.860 --> 01:03:03.195
so just sit back and watch, okay?

01:03:03.279 --> 01:03:05.155
You need to snap out of it.

01:03:09.076 --> 01:03:10.703
HEAVEN CAPITAL

01:03:11.078 --> 01:03:12.830
You sold it to them, didn't you?

01:03:12.997 --> 01:03:14.498
I'm going to get it back.

01:03:14.581 --> 01:03:15.874
You wait here.

01:03:17.918 --> 01:03:19.670
They'll kill you if you go there.

01:03:21.005 --> 01:03:22.131
Unbelievable.

01:03:26.552 --> 01:03:27.678
Good luck.

01:03:31.056 --> 01:03:32.224
Yes, come on in.

01:03:33.017 --> 01:03:34.852
All right, you can go now. Win big.

01:03:38.605 --> 01:03:39.648
How can I help you?

01:03:40.524 --> 01:03:42.484
My nephew used the house deed

01:03:42.568 --> 01:03:45.237
to borrow some money.

01:03:45.654 --> 01:03:47.072
I'll pay back the loan

01:03:47.156 --> 01:03:49.033
but you cannot sell that house.

01:03:49.491 --> 01:03:51.285
- You're here for the deed.
- Yes.

01:03:51.618 --> 01:03:53.454
- Have a seat.
- Oh, dear.

01:03:56.832 --> 01:03:57.833
What about the interest?

01:03:59.918 --> 01:04:01.253
He said he borrowed it just now.

01:04:01.337 --> 01:04:03.422
Just now? How long ago?

01:04:03.839 --> 01:04:05.132
An hour, maybe two.

01:04:05.382 --> 01:04:07.092
One or two hours. In that case

01:04:07.426 --> 01:04:10.179
for one hour, that's 3.6 million won

01:04:10.262 --> 01:04:13.098
and for two hours, it's 7.2 million.

01:04:13.432 --> 01:04:15.434
He just borrowed it.
How can it already be 7.2 million?

01:04:15.517 --> 01:04:17.978
Look, if you borrow money,
you have to pay the interest.

01:04:18.395 --> 01:04:20.481
What you're doing is completely illegal!

01:04:20.981 --> 01:04:23.984
Damn it. Why bring up
"illegal" in here, huh?

01:04:24.485 --> 01:04:26.570
Give it to me.
I need to leave with that deed.

01:04:28.947 --> 01:04:32.159
Why so many pains in the ass
these days, huh?

01:04:32.576 --> 01:04:34.328
Hey, you. Get up. You hear me?

01:04:37.081 --> 01:04:38.082
Mister.

01:04:39.041 --> 01:04:40.501
If you borrowed money

01:04:40.834 --> 01:04:42.169
you pay

01:04:42.336 --> 01:04:43.545
the interest. Got it?

01:04:43.629 --> 01:04:45.130
I just want the deed.

01:04:46.757 --> 01:04:47.800
This little...

01:04:49.176 --> 01:04:53.347
- Shut down the casinos!
- Shut them down!

01:04:53.430 --> 01:04:57.351
A casino in pristine
Yeongseon Island? It's unacceptable!

01:05:12.574 --> 01:05:15.619
ORAN CHINESE RESTAURANT

01:05:26.922 --> 01:05:28.757
What... Is he dead?

01:05:28.841 --> 01:05:30.884
Hey, get him out.

01:05:31.218 --> 01:05:32.553
Hey, mister.

01:05:32.845 --> 01:05:33.846
Go sleep it off at home.

01:05:35.055 --> 01:05:38.600
Never fall back!
A Republic warrior is never weak!

01:05:45.482 --> 01:05:48.444
That's right!
Rise up and destroy our enemies!

01:05:48.527 --> 01:05:50.195
The enemies of the Republic...

01:05:50.737 --> 01:05:54.324
- will be annihilated!
- Come on, get up.

01:05:54.408 --> 01:05:55.576
Come on, get up.

01:05:55.993 --> 01:05:57.536
I said go sleep it off at home.

01:06:05.711 --> 01:06:06.962
What's wrong with his eyes?

01:06:14.761 --> 01:06:15.804
What the hell?

01:06:19.683 --> 01:06:21.435
- What the hell?
- Who is this bastard?

01:07:44.977 --> 01:07:46.353
I finally found him.

01:07:47.813 --> 01:07:48.814
Bulgae.

01:07:51.400 --> 01:07:53.402
SPECIAL THANKS TO KIM SANG-KYUNG, KWON
YUL, AHN NAE-SANG, PARK JI-HWAN

01:07:53.485 --> 01:07:55.279
KIM JAE-HWA, KO KYU-PHIL, AND HAN
EUN-SEONG FOR THEIR SPECIAL APPEARANCES.

01:07:55.904 --> 01:07:58.323
FIFTIES PROFESSIONALS

01:08:10.335 --> 01:08:11.336
He's made his move.

01:08:11.420 --> 01:08:13.505
The guy we've been watching for ten years.

01:08:13.589 --> 01:08:15.382
She was no ordinary civilian.

01:08:15.465 --> 01:08:16.758
A 007 agent.

01:08:16.842 --> 01:08:19.094
I made sure she won't go

01:08:19.177 --> 01:08:20.804
near the case again.

01:08:21.054 --> 01:08:22.806
It's on the house for our regulars.

01:08:23.015 --> 01:08:24.016
Are you crazy?

01:08:24.099 --> 01:08:25.809
Did I go out and mess around like you did?

01:08:26.143 --> 01:08:28.729
You started this whole mess
over an island?

01:08:28.812 --> 01:08:30.355
I have a favor to ask.

01:08:30.439 --> 01:08:35.068
If we say Seong-won is dead,
the man Jeong Ho-myeong adores

01:08:35.569 --> 01:08:38.071
he'll show up at the funeral
no matter what.

01:08:38.155 --> 01:08:39.156
Boss!

01:08:39.656 --> 01:08:41.491
Now I'm sure of it.
